The UE shall:
- continue using the configuration used prior to when the inability to comply with the RRCReconfiguration message was detected;
- continue using the configuration used prior to the reception of RRCReconfiguration message;
- if MCG transmission is not suspended: initiate the SCG failure information procedure as specified in clause 5.7.3 to report SCG reconfiguration error, upon which the connection reconfiguration procedure ends;
- initiate the connection re-establishment procedure as specified in TS 36.331, clause 5.3.7, upon which the connection reconfiguration procedure ends.

A UE in RRC_CONNECTED may initiate the procedure to indicate it is interested in NR sidelink communication upon:

- Successful connection establishment or resuming;
- Change of interest;
- Changing QoS profiles;
- Receiving UECapabilityInformationSidelink from the associated peer UE;
- RLC mode information updated from the associated peer UE;
- Change to a PCell providing SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR;
- Configuration by upper layers to receive NR sidelink communication on a frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell, if the UE did not previously transmit a SidelinkUEInformationNR message or if the last transmission did not include sl-RxInterestedFreqList or if the frequency has changed since the last transmission.

A UE acting as U2N Relay UE may initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message for relay discovery announcements if:

- The UE is configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink L2 U2N relay discovery announcements on a frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell, and SIB12 includes sl-L2U2N-Relay;
- The UE has not previously transmitted a SidelinkUEInformationNR message since entering RRC_CONNECTED;
- Or, since the last transmission, the UE connected to a PCell not providing SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR or connected to a PCell providing SIB12 but not including sl-L2U2N-Relay;
- Or, the last transmission did not include sl-TxResourceReqListDisc;
- Or, the information carried by sl-TxResourceReqListDisc has changed since the last transmission;
- **AND** the U2N Relay UE threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.14.2 are met.

These conditions are derived from the context provided, specifically the section on initiating SidelinkUEInformationNR transmission for relay discovery announcements.

Upon reception of the RRCReject, the UE shall:

- Stop timer T300, if running;
- Stop timer T319, if running;
- Stop timer T319a, if running;
- Stop timer T302, if running;
- Reset MAC and release the default MAC Cell Group configuration;
- If waitTime is configured in the RRCReject: start timer T302 with the timer value set to the waitTime;
- If RRCReject is received in response to a request from upper layers: inform the upper layer that access barring is applicable for all access categories except categories '0' and '2';
- If RRCReject is received in response to an RRCSetupRequest: inform upper layers about the failure to setup the RRC connection, upon which the procedure ends;
- Else if RRCReject is received in response to an RRCResumeRequest or an RRCResumeRequest1:
  - If resume is triggered by upper layers: inform upper layers about the failure to resume the RRC connection;
  - If resume is triggered due to an RNA update, or if resume is triggered for SDT and T380 is not running: set the variable pendingRNA-Update to true;
  - Discard the current K key, the K key, the K key, the K key and the K key derived in gNB RRCenc RRCint UPint UPenc accordance with 5.3.13.3;
  - Suspend SRB1 and the radio bearers configured for SDT, if any;
  - For each radio bearer configured for SDT: indicate PDCP suspend to lower layers and re-establish the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322;
  - The procedure ends.

Additionally, for L2 U2N Relay UE: either trigger PC5-S release or send a Notification message to the connected L2 U2N Remote UE(s) in accordance with 5.8.9.10.

The RRC_INACTIVE UE shall continue to monitor paging while timer T302 is running. If timer T331 is running, the UE continues to perform idle/inactive measurements according to 5.7.8.

For each measObjectId included in the received measObjectToRemoveList that is part of measObjectList in VarMeasConfig, the UE shall:

1. Remove the entry with the matching measObjectId from the measObjectList within the VarMeasConfig;
2. Remove all measId associated with this measObjectId from the measIdList within the VarMeasConfig, if any;
3. If a measId is removed from the measIdList:
   - Remove the measurement reporting entry for this measId from the VarMeasReportList, if included;
   - Stop the periodical reporting timer or timer T321 or timer T322, whichever is running, and reset the associated information (e.g. timeToTrigger) for this measId.

For each condReconfigId received in the condReconfigToAddModList IE, the UE shall:

1. If an entry with the matching condReconfigId exists in the condReconfigToAddModList within the VarConditionalReconfig:
   - If the entry includes an condExecutionCond or condExecutionCondSCG, replace condExecutionCond or condExecutionCondSCG within the VarConditionalReconfig with the value received for this condReconfigId;
   - If the entry includes an condRRCReconfig, replace condRRCReconfig within the VarConditionalReconfig with the value received for this condReconfigId;
   - Add a new entry for this condReconfigId within the VarConditionalReconfig;
2. Perform conditional reconfiguration evaluation as specified in 5.3.5.13.4.

Upon reception of RRCReject, the UE shall:

- Stop timer T300, if running;  
- Stop timer T319, if running;  
- Stop timer T319a, if running;  
- Stop timer T302, if running;  
- Reset MAC and release the default MAC Cell Group configuration;  
- If waitTime is configured in the RRCReject: start timer T302 with the timer value set to the waitTime;  
- If RRCReject is received in response to a request from upper layers: inform the upper layer that access barring is applicable for all access categories except categories '0' and '2';  
- If RRCReject is received in response to an RRCSetupRequest: inform upper layers about the failure to setup the RRC connection, upon which the procedure ends;  
- Else if RRCReject is received in response to an RRCResumeRequest or an RRCResumeRequest1:  
  - If resume is triggered by upper layers: inform upper layers about the failure to resume the RRC connection;  
  - If resume is triggered due to an RNA update, or triggered for SDT and T380 is not running:  
    - Set the variable pendingRNA-Update to true;  
    - Discard the current K key, the K key, the K key, the K key and the K key derived in gNB RRCenc RRCint UPint UPenc accordance with 5.3.13.3;  
    - Suspend SRB1 and the radio bearers configured for SDT, if any;  
    - For each radio bearer configured for SDT:  
      - Indicate PDCP suspend to lower layers;  
      - Re-establish the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322;  
  - The procedure ends;  
- Upon L2 U2N Relay UE receiving RRCReject, it either triggers PC5-S release or sends a Notification message to the connected L2 U2N Remote UE(s) in accordance with 5.8.9.10;  
- The RRC_INACTIVE UE shall continue to monitor paging while timer T302 is running.

For each reportConfigId in reportConfigToRemoveList that is part of the current UE configuration in VarMeasConfig, the UE shall:

1. Remove the entry with the matching reportConfigId from the reportConfigList within the VarMeasConfig;
2. Remove all measId associated with the reportConfigId from the measIdList within the VarMeasConfig, if any;
3. If a measId is removed from the measIdList:
   - Remove the measurement reporting entry for this measId from the VarMeasReportList, if included;
   - Stop the periodical reporting timer or timer T321 or timer T322, whichever one is running, and reset the associated information (e.g. timeToTrigger) for this measId.

For each logicalChannelIdentity/LogicalChannelIdentityExt value included in the rlc-BearerToReleaseList/rlc-BearerToReleaseListExt that is part of the current UE configuration within the same cell group, the UE shall:  
2 > release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3;  
2 > release the corresponding logical channel.

Upon receiving a PUCCH release request from lower layers, for all bandwidth parts of an indicated serving cell the UE shall:  
1 > release PUCCH-CSI-Resources configured in CSI-ReportConfig;  
1 > release SchedulingRequestResourceConfig instances configured in PUCCH-Config.

If cell selection occurs while T390 is running, the UE shall:

- Stop T390 for all access categories;
- Perform the actions as specified in 5.3.14.4.

If the RRCReestablishment message includes the sl-L2RemoteUEConfig (i.e., the UE is a L2 U2N Remote UE), the UE shall:

- Perform the L2 U2N Remote UE configuration procedure as specified in 5.3.5.16;
- Consider the current cell to be the PCell.

Upon T311 expiry, if the procedure was initiated due to radio link failure or handover failure, the UE shall:

- set the `noSuitableCellFound` in the `VarRLF-Report` to `true`;
- perform the actions upon going to RRC_IDLE as specified in 5.3.11, with release cause 'RRC connection failure'.

For each sl-ReportConfigId in the received sl-ReportConfigToRemoveList that is part of the current UE configuration in VarMeasConfigSL, the UE shall:

1. Remove the entry with the matching sl-ReportConfigId from the sl-ReportConfigList within the VarMeasConfigSL;
2. Remove all sl-MeasId associated with the sl-ReportConfigId from the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL, if any;
3. If a sl-MeasId is removed from the sl-MeasIdList:
   - Remove the measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if included;
   - Stop the periodical reporting timer and reset the associated information (e.g. sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId.

If the resumption of the RRC connection is triggered by response to NG-RAN paging, the UE shall:

- Select '0' as the Access Category;
- Perform the unified access control procedure as specified in 5.3.14 using the selected Access Category and one or more Access Identities provided by upper layers.

When conditions for initiating SDT in accordance with 5.3.13.1b are fulfilled, the UE:

- Considers the resume procedure as initiated for SDT;
- Starts timer T319a;
- Starts timer T319;
- Instructs the MAC entity to consider the cg-SDT-TimeAlignmentTimer as expired, if it is running.

A UE in (NG)EN-DC executes a subclause of clause 5 in this specification when:

- the subclause is referred to from a subclause under execution, either in this specification or in TS 36.331;
- or the subclause applies to a message received on SRB3 (if SRB3 is established);
- or the subclause applies to field(s), IE(s), UE variable(s), or timer(s) in this specification that the UE is configured with.

If T304 of the MCG expires and any DAPS bearer is configured without radio link failure detected in the source PCell, the UE shall:

- reset MAC for the target PCell and release the MAC configuration for the target PCell;
- for each DAPS bearer:
  - release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the target PCell;
  - reconfigure the PDCP entity to release DAPS as specified in TS 38.323;
- for each SRB:
  - if the masterKeyUpdate was not received:
    - configure the PDCP entity for the source PCell with state variables continuation as specified in TS 38.323;
    - release the PDCP entity for the target PCell;
    - release the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the target PCell;
    - trigger the PDCP entity for the source PCell to perform SDU discard as specified in TS 38.323;
    - re-establish the RLC entity for the source PCell;
- release the physical channel configuration for the target PCell;
- discard the keys used in target PCell (the K_RRCenc, K_RRCint, K_UPenc, K_UPint, and gNB K_key), if any;
- resume suspended SRBs in the source PCell;
- revert back to the UE configuration used for the DRB or multicast MRB in the source PCell, including PDCP, RLC state variables, the security configuration and the data stored in transmission and reception buffers in PDCP and RLC entities;
- revert back to the UE measurement configuration used in the source PCell;
- store the handover failure information in VarRLF-Report as described in clause 5.3.10.5;
- initiate the failure information procedure as specified in clause 5.7.5 to report DAPS handover failure;
- revert back to the UE configuration used in the source PCell;
- if the associated T304 was not initiated upon cell selection performed while timer T311 was running, as defined in clause 5.3.7.3:
  - store the handover failure information in VarRLF-Report as described in clause

The UE shall consider an MBS service to be part of the MBS services of interest if the following conditions are met:

1. The UE is receiving or interested to receive this service via a broadcast MRB;  
2. The session of this service is ongoing or about to start;  
3. One or more MBS FSAIs in the USD for this service is included in SIB21 acquired from the PCell for a frequency belonging to the set of MBS frequencies of interest, determined according to 5.9.4.3.

The UE shall acquire the MIB when:

- The UE is in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE;
- The UE is in RRC_CONNECTED while T311 is running;
- The UE is in RRC_CONNECTED with an active BWP having a common search space configured by searchSpaceSIB1 and pagingSearchSpace, and has received an indication about a change of system information;
- The UE is in RRC_CONNECTED with an active BWP having a common search space configured by searchSpaceSIB1, and has not stored a valid version of a required SIB or posSIB, or has not acquired SIB1 in the current modification period;
- The UE is in RRC_CONNECTED with an active BWP having a common search space configured by searchSpaceSIB1, and si-BroadcastStatus or posSIB-BroadcastStatus for required SIB(s) or posSIB(s) is set to notbroadcasting in the acquired SIB1 in the current modification period.

Additionally, the UE shall acquire the MIB if it is unable to acquire the SIB1, as specified in clause 5.2.2.5, and in other cases where SIB1 acquisition is required and ssb-SubcarrierOffset indicates SIB1 is transmitted in the cell.

If the current configuration contains a BH RLC Channel with the received bh-RLC-ChannelID within the same cell group, the IAB-node shall:

- If reestablishRLC is received: re-establish the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322;
- Reconfigure the RLC entity or entities in accordance with the received rlc-Config;
- Reconfigure the logical channel in accordance with the received mac-LogicalChannelConfig.

Upon reception of an RRCReconfigurationFailureSidelink, the UE shall:

1. Stop timer T400 for the destination, if running;
2. Continue using the configuration used prior to the corresponding RRCReconfigurationSidelink message;
3. Perform the sidelink UE information for NR sidelink communication procedure, as specified in 5.8.3.3 or clause 5.10.15 in TS 36.331.

For each DAPS bearer, when the RRCReconfiguration includes `daps-SourceRelease`, the UE shall:

- Release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the source SpCell;
- Reconfigure the PDCP entity to release DAPS as specified in TS 38.323.

When the RRCReconfiguration includes `daps-SourceRelease`, the UE shall:

- Release the PDCP entity for the target PCell;  
- Release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the target PCell;  
- Reconfigure the PDCP entity to release DAPS as specified in TS 38.323;  
- Trigger the PDCP entity for the source PCell to perform SDU discard as specified in TS 38.323;  
- Re-establish the RLC entity for the source PCell.

Additionally, the UE shall:
- Revert back to the UE configuration used in the source PCell, including PDCP, RLC state variables, security configuration, and data stored in transmission and reception buffers in PDCP and RLC entities.

This applies to all SRBs associated with the DAPS bearer being released.

The UE shall:  
- derive or update the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) based on the KgNB key and using the received sk-Counter value, as specified in TS 33.501;  
- derive the K and K keys as specified in TS 33.501 using the ciphering algorithms indicated in the RadioBearerConfig associated with the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) as indicated by keyToUse;  
- derive the K and K keys as specified in TS 33.501 using the integrity protection algorithms indicated in the RadioBearerConfig associated with the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) as indicated by keyToUse.

The UE shall:  
- consider inter-RAT mobility as initiated towards UTRA-FDD;  
- forward the nas-SecurityParamFromNR to the upper layers, if included;  
- access the target cell indicated in the inter-RAT message in accordance with the specifications of the target RAT.
